<p>If you're not familiar with backtracking, it might be useful to review t=
he <em>Backtracking</em> chapter before continuing with this problem.</p>
<p><strong>Original problem - words array contains multiple words</strong><=
br>
<!-- -->The above approach works well for one word, but repeating this proc=
ess for every word in the array is quite expensive. Let=E2=80=99s devise a =
way to make our search more efficient. Consider the following board:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
